\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come to our poor nature's night
\par With Thy blessed inward light,
\par Holy Ghost the Infinite,
\par Comforter devine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. We are sinful-cleanse us, Lord;
\par Sick and faint-Thy strength afford;
\par Lost, until by Thee restored,
\par Comforter divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Like the dew Thy peace distil;
\par Guide, subdue our wayward will,
\par Things of Christ unfolding still,
\par Comforter divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Gentle, awful, holy Guest,
\par Make Thy temple in each breast;
\par There Thy presence be confessed, 
\par Comforter divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. With us, for us, intercede,
\par And, with voiceless groanings, plead
\par Our unutterable need,
\par Comforter divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. In us Abba, Father! Cry,
\par Earnest of the bliss on high,
\par Seal of immortality,
\par Comforter divine.\tab\tab 
\par                    Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

